WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.134
-Junior, I am the number-two

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.770
Executive Vice President
at Santa Inc.,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.173
who only answers to Santa,
Brent, and the board.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.841
I can end that nose of yours.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.477
-I'd like to see you try.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.511
A lot of powerful people
need this nose to glow

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:13.946
so they can pay their mortgages

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.581
and send their kids
to private school.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.283
So, by all means, go ahead

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.986
and try to stop this nose
from glowing.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.522
-God damn it. You're right.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.424
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Sarah Silverman.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.026
That was a clip from
your new show, "Santa Inc."

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.561
-Yes.
-Not for kids.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.963
-No.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.497
-Yeah.
-Not for kids.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.265
-It looks like it might be
for kids, but then you hear

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:34.633
a "God damn it"
at the end of the clip,

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.802
and you're like, "Oh,
this is from Sarah Silverman."

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:38.504
-I mean, I think
it's the kind of thing

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:42.008
you want kids
to watch anyway, maybe?

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.142
-Like, cool kids.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.877
You want a cool kid
to find their way to it,

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.446
right, that can handle it.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.980
-What is the premise
of "Santa Inc."?

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.350
-It's like the business
of Christmas.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.284
It takes place
in the North Pole.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:55.421
And it's, like, the year-round
business of getting ready

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:58.825
for that one night of Christmas,
and it's funny.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.394
It's made entirely --
not entirely --

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:05.164
but many Jews came together
to create this.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.499
Seth Rogen and me

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:10.436
and the creator and writer,
Ali Rushfield and --

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.006
But first of all, the elves.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:16.276
I play an elf. Candy Smalls.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:21.414
And elves are Jews in this.
They're Jew--

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.017
Because they can work Christmas
and...

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.451
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.320
I think really elves are Jews.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.754
-Yeah.
-I mean, like,

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:31.090
you know, there's no Christmas
without Jews.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.328
Like, every Christmas song
you love is -- Jews wrote it.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:38.898
Like, every single one.
It's crazy, these Jews.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.435
-Yeah.
-I just made it other.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.270
-But that's a very true thing,
that this --

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.873
You're not just making something
up about these Christmas songs.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.774
There are a lot of famous
Jewish songwriters.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:52.011
-Every Christmas song you love
is written by a Jewish person.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.479
-Yeah.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.814
-And Christmas specials and --
Yeah. I mean --

00:01:55.814 --> 00:01:57.483
-Did you grow up
loving Christmas

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.218
or did you not
celebrate it at all

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:01.287
and had no take on it
one way or the other?

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.656
-We totally did Christmas
because I grew up

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.258
in New Hampshire,
in Bedford, New Hampshire.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.126
Same as you, and so, you know,

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.328
Hanukkah is like
the Jewish Christmas,

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.597
but it's not a --
If you're, like, Jewy --

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:15.968
If you're very Jewish,
it's not a big holiday.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.304
They just make it that way
so kids aren't bummed

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.573
when they live in New Hampshire
and everyone has Christmas.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.575
But, yeah, we had, like,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.610
a Christmas Hanukkah "bush."

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:27.347
You know? Whatever. But, um --

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.782
Yeah. There's no -- Listen.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.817
Christmas has become --

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:35.254
And I think this talks --
The show speaks to it a bit.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:38.458
You know, about
it's stuff and things,

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.494
but at its core,
it's about the birth

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.330
of the nicest Jewish boy ever.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.233
You know? Like...
You know.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.701
The only caveat is, like --

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.436
The only disagreement maybe
is Jews

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:55.274
are disappointed that he became
a messiah and not a doctor.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:57.744
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.178
You know.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.546
-Speaking of very nice
Jewish boys,

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:01.848
your co-star is Seth Rogen.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.550
He's right at the top
of that list, right?

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.751
-Yes.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.019
-I mean, how did you
first meet Seth Rogen?

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:09.388
-You know what?
I didn't remember this.

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:12.558
But I did -- He does this thing
every year with his wife,

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.861
Lauren Miller,
called Hilarity for Charity.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:21.000
He does, like, a stand-up thing
for Alzheimer's and, um --

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.968
Sorry.
I'm, like, really scattered.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.603
And I just remembered
a joke my dad --

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:27.140
It's, like, an old joke
that my dad just told me about.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.541
I'll just say it in two seconds.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:33.012
The doctor says, "I've got
bad news and worse news."

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:36.648
He says, "What's the bad news?"
"Uh, you have cancer."

00:03:36.648 --> 00:03:37.850
He goes,
"What's the other news?"

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.086
"You have Alzheimer's."
And he's like, "Oh, God.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.154
Well, at least
I don't have cancer."

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:43.323
Anyway.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.757
It made me think of them,
and then I laughed,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.825
and then I felt like
I had to explain it.

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:50.830
So, Seth -- I'm telling
other people's jokes.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.699
-I love it. Via your father,
which is wonderful.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.267
I mean, unlike your dog,

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.570
I believe your father does like
this show, so this is great.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.038
-He loves it.
-Very good.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:02.508
-They just texted me like,
"We're recording 'Seth.'"

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:06.445
They don't talk --
Yeah, they do talk...

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:09.081
How I met Seth Rogen --
I didn't know,

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:12.217
but he introduced me
at Hilarity for Charity

00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:16.788
as the first famous person
he ever smoked pot with.

00:04:16.788 --> 00:04:18.390
And I was like --
I got on stage,

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.525
and I was like, "Is that true?"

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.127
Because we've worked
together since.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.561
We played brother and sister

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.096
in a movie called
"take this waltz"

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.733
and we did
this short film together

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.000
and blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.870
And we've just known
each other through comedy.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.906
Anyway, he said, "Yeah,"
and what it was

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.808
was when I was first
doing stand-up

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.342
at the Hollywood Improv,

00:04:37.342 --> 00:04:40.613
I was in my early 20s, mid 20s.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.850
And I guess he was probably
like 18 or something.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:48.053
And there was a kid that would
come around who was like 18,

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:50.289
and he'd come around
in his, like, car

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.358
and be like,
"Do you want to smoke pot?"

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.659
And I'd be like, "Yeah."

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:56.729
And I'd get in
and drive around with him.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:59.498
He actually grew up to be
a wonderful writer/director,

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.667
this kid Jonathan Kasdan.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.836
But Seth was there
one of those times.

00:05:04.836 --> 00:05:08.840
But he was just, like, a kid
that I smoked pot with.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.777
-Well, that's really nice

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.945
that you could have
that experience with him.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:16.048
-You shouldn't get in cars
with strangers with drugs.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:18.050
You know, but I could
absolutely take him,

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.453
so I didn't feel scared.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.022
I also think, like, kids
shouldn't get in cars

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.457
with, like, famous people
to smoke weed, either.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:27.893
I mean, like --
-Right.

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:29.962
Well, they had the weed.
-They did have the weed.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.864
You know what?
You're off the hook this time.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:32.998
-Thank you.

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:34.533
-Hey, you guys,
that's Sarah Silverman.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.268
New episodes of
"The Sarah Silverman Podcast"

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:37.936
are released on Thursdays,
and "Santa Inc."

00:05:37.936 --> 00:05:40.406
premieres December 7th
on HBO Max.

